    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="0905" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/923</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hartman to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-16T11:00:00-05:14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s March 13, 6 p.m. Limited construction work continuing on new
                    railways. Information of British Chargé d’Affaires was received from the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs in two interviews. In second interview the Minister
                    is reported by British Chargé d’Affaires as stating that the President of
                    Ecuador, the Minister of Hacienda, and the Minister of the Interior fully
                    concurred with him. I regard the statements of the Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    and the British Chargé d’Affaires as entirely reliable and trustworthy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
